### TeamForge Phase 14 API Tests (REST Client Format)
### Mentor Lifecycle: Abandonment Review, First-Week Activity, Re-application Cooldown, Mentee Cap, Post-Session Feedback

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@ownerToken = Bearer YOUR_OWNER_TOKEN_HERE
@mentorToken = Bearer YOUR_MENTOR_TOKEN_HERE
@collabToken = Bearer YOUR_COLLABORATOR_TOKEN_HERE
@adminToken = Bearer YOUR_ADMIN_TOKEN_HERE
@superUserToken = Bearer YOUR_SUPERUSER_TOKEN_HERE

### --------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1. MENTOR ABANDONMENT REVIEW & ACTIVITY LIFECYCLE
### --------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 1a. Owner Checks Mentor Activity & Review Status
# Expected Status: 200 OK
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/PROJECT_ID/mentor/abandonment-review
Authorization: {{ownerToken}}

###

### 1b. Collaborator Attempts to Check Mentor Abandonment Review
# Expected Status: 403 Forbidden
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/PROJECT_ID/mentor/abandonment-review
Authorization: {{collabToken}}

###

### 1c. Owner Opens Abandonment Review (Rejected if Mentor Active Within 7 Days)
# Expected Status: 201 Created (or 409 MENTOR_STILL_ACTIVE / REVIEW_COOLDOWN / REVIEW_ALREADY_OPEN)
POST {{baseUrl}}/projects/PROJECT_ID/mentor/abandonment-review
Authorization: {{ownerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "Mentor has been unresponsive for over a week."
}

###

### 1d. Mentor Fetches Open Abandonment Reviews Requiring Confirmation
# Expected Status: 200 OK
GET {{baseUrl}}/mentor/abandonment-reviews/mine
Authorization: {{mentorToken}}

###

### 1e. Assigned Mentor Confirms They Are Still Active (Logs Activity & Restarts 7-Day Clock)
# Expected Status: 200 OK
POST {{baseUrl}}/mentor/abandonment-reviews/REVIEW_ID/confirm
Authorization: {{mentorToken}}

###

### 1f. Admin Cancels an Open Abandonment Review (Requires Written Reason)
# Expected Status: 200 OK (400 REASON_REQUIRED if reason omitted)
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/abandonment-reviews/REVIEW_ID/cancel
Authorization: {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "Mentor contacted support regarding scheduled medical leave."
}

###

### 1g. Save Session Note (Records Mentor Project Activity)
# Expected Status: 200 OK
POST {{baseUrl}}/mentor-sessions/SESSION_ID/notes
Authorization: {{mentorToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "note": "Reviewed architecture diagrams and agreed on weekly milestone deliverables."
}

###

### --------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2. MENTEE CAPACITY CAP & BOOKING
### --------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 2a. Mentor Sets Max Active Mentees (1 to 10, Default 3)
# Expected Status: 200 OK
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/mentor-marketplace/mentors/profile
Authorization: {{mentorToken}}
x-user-id: 7
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "maxActiveMentees": 3
}

###

### 2b. Book Session Beyond Mentor Active Mentee Cap
# Expected Status: 409 Conflict (Code: MENTOR_AT_CAPACITY)
POST {{baseUrl}}/mentor-marketplace/sessions/book
Authorization: {{ownerToken}}
x-user-id: 1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "mentorId": "mentor-profile-1",
  "projectId": "PROJECT_ID",
  "topic": "Milestone Architecture Review",
  "scheduledAt": "2026-06-01T10:00:00.000Z"
}

###

### --------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 3. RE-APPLICATION COOLDOWN AFTER REJECTION
### --------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 3a. Re-apply Before Cooldown Expires (Default 14 Days)
# Expected Status: 409 Conflict (Code: REAPPLY_COOLDOWN with availableAt)
POST {{baseUrl}}/mentor-applications
Authorization: {{collabToken}}
x-user-id: 2
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "2",
  "email": "arjun.sharma@teamforge.io",
  "name": "Arjun Sharma",
  "years": 6,
  "bio": "Experienced backend and distributed systems engineer mentoring teams.",
  "skills": ["Node.js", "TypeScript", "NestJS"],
  "cvFileName": "cv-arjun.pdf",
  "certificates": [
    {
      "title": "AWS Certified Solutions Architect",
      "issuer": "Amazon Web Services",
      "holderName": "Arjun Sharma",
      "documentNumber": "AWS-991"
    }
  ]
}

###

### --------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 4. POST-SESSION FEEDBACK (PRIVATE TO OWNER -> ADMIN + AGGREGATE STATS)
### --------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 4a. Owner Submits 1-5 Private Feedback on Completed Session
# Expected Status: 200 OK (400 INVALID_RATING outside 1..5; 409 ALREADY_RATED on second call)
POST {{baseUrl}}/mentor-sessions/SESSION_ID/feedback
Authorization: {{ownerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "rating": 5,
  "comment": "Actionable feedback and very structured session notes."
}

###

### 4b. Mentor Fetches Own Private Aggregate Stats (No Single Comments / Student Names)
# Expected Status: 200 OK
GET {{baseUrl}}/mentor-marketplace/mentors/me/stats
Authorization: {{mentorToken}}

###

### 4c. Admin Inspects Full Mentor Feedback & Abandonment History
# Expected Status: 200 OK
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/mentors/7/feedback
Authorization: {{adminToken}}

###

### --------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 5. HOURLY SCHEDULER TICK & ESCROW RECONCILIATION
### --------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 5a. Trigger Hourly Tick (Includes mentorAbandonmentReleaser & mentorActivityNotifier)
# Expected Status: 202 Accepted
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/jobs/tick
Authorization: {{superUserToken}}

###

### 5b. Reconcile Escrow Across All Mentor Sessions
# Expected Status: 200 OK (ok: true, mismatches: [])
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/escrow/reconcile
Authorization: {{adminToken}}
